[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own table already
shows two causes, and a desk note under it flags reports that moved by one day. Counted per
report, the ticket holds three problems. The queued parser fix only covers the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Shipping the parser fix and closing #4471 leaves two problems open, with no ticket of their own until now.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} {labels} />

## How to tell them apart

Read the date in the report, then look up the tenant and how the report came in.

- **Day and month swapped** (7 April shows as 4 July). Came in by app, email or the booking-v2
  form: the **parser** problem. The tenant writes the day first and the shared parser reads
  month first.
- **Day and month swapped**, but it came in through the **booking-v3 form**: the **hint**
  problem. The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, people type what it says, and the form reads it day
  first. It looks exactly like the parser problem, so only the channel tells them apart.
- **One day off** (Tuesday shows as Monday, or two people see different days): the
  **shift** problem. Swapping day and month can't produce this. It points to time zones, which is an
  inference until someone reproduces it.

## Why one ticket hid three

- The subject doesn't separate them. #4471 took in "wrong day" reports under many different
  subjects, and the same subject turns up in all three problems. Matching on subject
  ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) and "when unsure, merge"
  ([triage](/kb/triage/dedupe)) both pull them together.
- Intake tags each report from the reporter's browser, not the tenant. On #4471 the tags
  disagree with the cause both ways, so neither the tag nor the subject can split the
  ticket. The tenant directory and the channel can.
- The export repeats reports where its pages overlap. Count by id: the table above does.

## What to do

- Keep the queued parser fix on [#1](https://github.com/MitchLillie/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1).
- Fix the booking-v3 date hint: [#2](https://github.com/MitchLillie/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2).
- Reproduce the one-day shift across time zones: [#3](https://github.com/MitchLillie/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3).
  One reporter says they stopped reporting it, so its count is a floor.
- When a big ticket's table shows more than one cause, split the ticket before marking it known.

